# R and a word typed at once, from a fresh launch, at 1120x780 (the owner's window size, with the reading
# pane showing the conversation under the cursor). The word must end up in the reply, which must be on
# screen with the caret in it (MAIL-UX K12, T38).
name r-fresh
size 1120 780
wait 1
expect windowSize contains 1120x
# nothing has the caret: the window is the first responder. The driver cannot click a row to make the list
# the first responder; the monitor takes R the same either way (it only steps aside for a text field).
expect firstResponder is MailKeyDriverWindow
expect mail.cursor is q3
expect mail.pane is q3
expect composer.title absent
shot before-R
type rEach
wait 1.5
expect composer.title is Reply
expect composer.host is q3
expect composer.to is sam@lee.example
expect composer.body is Each
expect composer.queued absent
expect composer.awaitingCaret is false
expect firstResponder contains mail.composer.body
expect mail.counts.inbox is 40
expect toast absent
shot reply-on-screen
# R again on the conversation he left a draft in: the draft reopens and a word typed at once goes after
# the text it already has
key escape
wait 0.5
expect composer.title absent
expect mail.counts.drafts is 1
type rThanks
wait 1.5
expect composer.title is Reply
expect composer.body is EachThanks
expect firstResponder contains mail.composer.body
shot reopened-draft
key escape
